  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "f1-tidy-commit-cannot-carry-records",
      "class": "blocking",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.agents/skills/joycraft-session-end/SKILL.md:55-56",
      "criterion": "spec-25-2",
      "summary": "New text says the tidy commit 'carries the records and the tidy fixes'. cleanup.mjs tidyVerify (payload/.joycraft/runtime/cleanup.mjs:691-711) refuses any changed file that no fixable finding names, and any untracked file. Fixture: a branch repo with one uncommitted decision-log line (a record) gives tidy --verify status 'refused', 'No fixable tidy finding names this file.', exit 2, message null (receipt spec-25-tidy-verify-record-edit.txt). So on a clean tree with a finished queue, any record the Records step writes (status --fix frontmatter, decision-log answer, knowledge row, new spec) blocks the one tidy commit, and the skill gives no other step that commits the records; with no tidy findings there is no message to commit with either. Fix: commit the records in their own commit before tidy (tidy then reads the new HEAD), or let tidy --verify ignore record paths; then drop 'it carries the records'."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2-archive-commit-judged",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.agents/skills/joycraft-session-end/SKILL.md:101",
      "assumption": "Decision session-end-push-order fixes one push and one CI run, not one commit; 'one tidy commit' names the tidy commit only.",
      "summary": "Implementer's gap judged correct: archive --apply moves folders with renameSync (archive.mjs:562,602-603) and makes no commit, so 'After --apply, commit the move' is needed and a second commit in the one push agrees with the decision. Consider naming its message and noting it also holds any --rewrite edits."
    },
    {
      "id": "f3-dirty-tree-which-steps",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.agents/skills/joycraft-session-end/SKILL.md:9-11",
      "assumption": "On a dirty tree, steps run in preview/read-only form: status.mjs without --fix, prune and archive previews only, no lease change.",
      "summary": "Dirty tree: 'report what the steps below find, fix nothing' does not say how to run steps whose commands write (status.mjs --fix, worktrees.mjs prune --apply, archive --apply, the joycraft-cleanup session-end mode). An agent may still run --fix or --apply. Name the read-only form of each step for this case."
    },
    {
      "id": "f4-no-remote",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.agents/skills/joycraft-session-end/SKILL.md:105-107",
